{"kind":"assert","text":"E5 ruling on the three shapes, from notes/2026-11-14-act-environment.md.\n\nComposition: no public ScopeClient composition method. Section 8.1 places composition on the environment surface as env.submit([a, b]). E5 may build the internal support on the retainAuthorizations batch, with keys and prior versions from checked Explore. The public method arrives with the ActEnvironment surface, so ScopeClient keeps one public submit.\n\nWaits: approved. Add one request-list arm for an unsigned authorization. It carries its exact authorization position, its authored input, and its waits or source status, under its own discriminant. It shows no custody occurrence and no AskedOf value. Item-row refs stay with E3. Section 15 notes that \"E5 owns the waits\", and this arm is how a page shows them.\n\nUnavailable via: it stays a pre-retention source stop. When the hypothetical prefix cannot supply a checked selector, the submit stops with source before retention and signing and writes nothing (decision 63f034d9). Add no immediate returned input. When the source records, the same submit takes the ordinary path.\n\nRecord all three answers in the E5 section of the note when the head lands.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}